WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.235
-Our next guest is an
Emmy Award-winning actress

00:00:03.235 --> 00:00:04.637
you know best from
her work on the

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.038
critically acclaimed series
"Killing Eve."

00:00:06.038 --> 00:00:07.240
She stars in "Free Guy,"

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.509
which premieres in theaters
on August 13th.

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:10.810
Let's take a look.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:13.212
-♪ It's such
a sweet, sweet fantasy, baby ♪

00:00:13.212 --> 00:00:14.847
-You know,
people say it all the time,

00:00:14.847 --> 00:00:16.616
like, "Guy can take [bleep]
in the face

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:17.917
better than anybody I know."

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:19.919
[ Laughs ]
I mean, when you put in that...

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:24.423
-♪ But it's just a
sweet, sweet fantasy, baby ♪

00:00:24.423 --> 00:00:29.195
♪ When I close my eyes,
you come and take me ♪

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:31.397
♪ On and on and on ♪

00:00:31.397 --> 00:00:33.232
-Don't have a good day.
Have a great day.

00:00:33.232 --> 00:00:34.633
-I love that song.

00:00:34.633 --> 00:00:36.102
[ Music stops ]

00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:39.772
-That's a new one.

00:00:39.772 --> 00:00:41.941
-Please welcome back
to the show Jodie Comer.

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:43.442
How are you, Jodie?

00:00:43.442 --> 00:00:44.543
-Hey, Seth. I'm good.
How are you?

00:00:44.543 --> 00:00:45.979
-I'm wonderful.

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:49.215
It's so nice to see you again.
This is a really fun movie.

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:50.783
Very different from what

00:00:50.783 --> 00:00:52.952
we have come to see from you
in "Killing Eve."

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:54.988
What made you
want to do this project?

00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:56.555
-Oh, my God.

00:00:56.555 --> 00:00:58.424
Well, I think the first thing
was the opportunity

00:00:58.424 --> 00:01:01.861
to work with Shawn Levy and
Ryan Reynolds, you know?

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:05.297
I knew that it was going to be
a tremendous amount of fun,

00:01:05.297 --> 00:01:07.066
and to read the script,
you know,

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:09.135
it was a new kind of
fresh concept.

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:11.437
It had a lot of imagination.

00:01:11.437 --> 00:01:13.072
And I didn't know how
they were going to execute it.

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:15.508
So it was such a joy
to be a part of.

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:19.679
-And really just
a face-altering wig, Jodie.

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:22.181
I mean, that's as unrecognizable

00:01:22.181 --> 00:01:24.050
as I could think
that a wig would make you.

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:26.486
-It deserves
its own credit, Seth.

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:31.124
No, me and that wig --
we have come a long way.

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:33.125
I remember when
we started filming --

00:01:33.125 --> 00:01:35.662
Before we started filming,
we had costume

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:39.866
and hair fittings, and there was
like five wigs in the running.

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:41.133
Four of them are great,

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:43.235
one I wasn't so keen on,
and I was just like,

00:01:43.235 --> 00:01:44.537
"You know what, guys?

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:47.006
There's just no way.
We shouldn't photograph this.

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:48.674
We should just, you know,
send the other four."

00:01:48.674 --> 00:01:51.310
And they were like, "No, no,
we should photograph it

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:52.778
and we should put it
with the four,

00:01:52.778 --> 00:01:54.047
because there's just
no way they're going to

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:56.516
pick this when
they see the rest of them."

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:58.885
So I was like, "Okay, then."
[ Laughs ]

00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:00.286
And then it was
like two days later,

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:03.823
and they all kind of came to me
in the makeup trailer

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:05.391
and just gave me a look.

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:08.127
And I was like, "They chose
the wig, didn't they?"

00:02:08.127 --> 00:02:10.797
They were like, "Yeah."

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:12.498
So, yeah, we've come a long way.

00:02:12.498 --> 00:02:13.832
-Yeah.
-We've come a long way.

00:02:13.832 --> 00:02:17.871
-Jodie, you forgot the
first rule of show business --

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:21.340
never let them take a picture of
you in the wig you don't like.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:23.776
-Seth, now I know.

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:25.177
This is the last time.

00:02:25.177 --> 00:02:28.715
-Did you ever use it
for the purposes of anonymity?

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:30.383
I mean, you could walk around,
I feel like,

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:34.053
with that wig and get away with
being Jodie Comer.

00:02:34.053 --> 00:02:35.488
-I haven't, unfortunately.

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:39.292
My friend -- Actually, my friend
who I spoke to you last time,

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:41.994
the Bruce Springsteen friend --
she came in to Boston

00:02:41.994 --> 00:02:45.532
to visit and she had it on
in the trailer

00:02:45.532 --> 00:02:48.901
while she was there, so I've got
a few novelty pictures of her.

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:52.171
She looks about 45,
which is brilliant.

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:53.439
Yeah.

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:55.708
-I think people would assume,
based on your work

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:58.210
as an assassin in "Killing Eve,"
that would be

00:02:58.210 --> 00:03:00.313
the most stunts you would
do in a project,

00:03:00.313 --> 00:03:01.413
but you actually had to do
a fair amount of

00:03:01.413 --> 00:03:02.414
stunt work in this.

00:03:02.414 --> 00:03:04.250
Maybe more intense?

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:05.518
-Yeah, I think so.

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:07.820
Like, I think people
tend to think "Killing Eve"

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:09.855
is very stunt-heavy,
but it isn't.

00:03:09.855 --> 00:03:13.392
But, no, on this, like,
when I went to Boston,

00:03:13.392 --> 00:03:15.795
it was like three hours a day
with the stunt department.

00:03:15.795 --> 00:03:19.665
And I was so eager to do
as much as I possibly could.

00:03:19.665 --> 00:03:21.233
Of course, I had
an incredible stunt double

00:03:21.233 --> 00:03:23.335
called Hayley Wright.

00:03:23.335 --> 00:03:26.572
But, yeah, I was
desperate to be cool.

00:03:26.572 --> 00:03:28.641
-But you -- Did I hear correctly

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:32.411
that you got kicked
in the face, Jodie?

00:03:32.411 --> 00:03:34.747
-I did.
I did get kicked in the face.

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:36.883
There was a -- There was an
accident in a stunt,

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:38.817
and I did get kicked
in the face.

00:03:38.817 --> 00:03:40.252
And it was very sobering.

00:03:40.252 --> 00:03:43.689
And -- But I also
do believe that everyone

00:03:43.689 --> 00:03:46.058
should get kicked in their face
at least once in their life.

00:03:46.058 --> 00:03:47.159
-Yeah, well,
you filmed in Boston,

00:03:47.159 --> 00:03:50.262
so you're not the first person.

00:03:50.262 --> 00:03:54.166
In Boston, that's a form of
affectionate greeting.

00:03:54.166 --> 00:03:55.902
-Yeah. It's like, in Glasgow,

00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:58.270
a head butt is called
a "Glasgow Kiss."

00:03:58.270 --> 00:03:59.272
-Right.
-Yeah.

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:01.774
-That's called a "Fenway Hello."

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:03.309
-Yeah.

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:08.114
-I would imagine
that, being from Liverpool,

00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:11.183
that would be a place
that is very taken aback

00:04:11.183 --> 00:04:13.452
when people try to do
a Liverpool accent

00:04:13.452 --> 00:04:14.753
and get it wrong.

00:04:14.753 --> 00:04:16.122
Boston, obviously,
is very similar.

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:18.057
Did you -- Would you even
attempt to do

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:20.660
a Boston accent
after spending time there?

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:23.796
-I've tried
and I failed miserably.

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:25.831
It's really, really hard to do.

00:04:25.831 --> 00:04:28.133
And I actually think Bostonians
are quite precious,

00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:31.036
like Scousers are
with the Liverpool accent.

00:04:31.036 --> 00:04:34.007
Like, if someone doesn't do it
right, they really --

00:04:34.007 --> 00:04:35.775
they really make sure
that you know

00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:37.477
that you didn't do it right.

00:04:37.477 --> 00:04:40.279
So I found a fair amount of
that in the --

00:04:40.279 --> 00:04:43.983
-Yeah. They're not a coy people.

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:45.751
-They're not shy. No, no, no.
-No.

00:04:45.751 --> 00:04:47.052
-But I love that. I love that.

00:04:47.052 --> 00:04:51.924
-A famously opinionated stock,
the Bostonians.

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:55.261
And I want to ask, as well --

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:56.929
I know you are doing
a fourth season now --

00:04:56.929 --> 00:05:00.266
are you excited about what we're
going to see with "Killing Eve"?

00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:02.434
-Yes, I am.

00:05:02.434 --> 00:05:05.171
We're halfway through Season 4.

00:05:05.171 --> 00:05:06.639
I obviously can't say much,

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:09.041
but we've definitely got off
to an exciting start.

00:05:09.041 --> 00:05:13.178
I think now that, because we
know that it's the final season,

00:05:13.178 --> 00:05:15.882
they're definitely
kind of pushing boundaries,

00:05:15.882 --> 00:05:17.316
especially with Villanelle.

00:05:17.316 --> 00:05:20.252
You know, where we kind of
open up with her is

00:05:20.252 --> 00:05:23.189
bonkers and kind of brilliant.

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:26.658
So, yeah, I hope people enjoy
when it finally hits the screen.

00:05:26.658 --> 00:05:28.060
-I mean, is -- Are you --

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:30.028
You know, you mentioned
it is the final season.

00:05:30.028 --> 00:05:31.463
You know, this was such a

00:05:31.463 --> 00:05:33.733
transformative part for you,
personally.

00:05:33.733 --> 00:05:35.435
Like, have you been
mourning the fact that

00:05:35.435 --> 00:05:39.004
you are saying
goodbye to Villanelle?

00:05:39.004 --> 00:05:41.407
-Not yet,
because I can't let myself.

00:05:41.407 --> 00:05:43.576
I have like
two whole months left.

00:05:43.576 --> 00:05:45.143
I had, like,
a little moment the other day

00:05:45.143 --> 00:05:47.713
where I seen the clapper board
and I had, like, this

00:05:47.713 --> 00:05:49.348
kind of lump in my throat
and I was like,

00:05:49.348 --> 00:05:52.017
"Gosh, I've got a whole other
two months to go."

00:05:52.017 --> 00:05:53.286
It's like a marathon.

00:05:53.286 --> 00:05:55.521
Like, you can't think --
If you're at the start line,

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:57.089
you can't think of the finish.

00:05:57.089 --> 00:05:58.590
Not that I've ever run
a marathon,

00:05:58.590 --> 00:05:59.725
but that's what I imagine.

00:05:59.725 --> 00:06:01.627
-No, I think you got it.
I think you got it.

00:06:01.627 --> 00:06:03.296
And if you do ever
run a marathon,

00:06:03.296 --> 00:06:05.965
we would like to request
you do it in that wig.

00:06:05.965 --> 00:06:08.034
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:08.034 --> 00:06:10.002
For you, I will.

00:06:10.002 --> 00:06:11.871
-Thank you.
-I will.

00:06:11.871 --> 00:06:14.106
-Hey, it's always
so lovely to see you, Jodie.

00:06:14.106 --> 00:06:15.908
Congratulations on everything,
and hopefully, next time,

00:06:15.908 --> 00:06:17.042
we will see you in person.

00:06:17.042 --> 00:06:20.145
-Thanks so much, Seth.
-Alright, be well.

00:06:20.145 --> 00:06:21.547
"Free Guy" is this theaters
this Friday.

